  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3003.07 Revocation of A Hardship Registration",
  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3003.07 Revocation of A Hardship Registration.\n\n(a) Upon receipt of evidence indicating that a person who has obtained a hardship registration for the vehicle has operated said vehicle, the bureau of hearings shall provide an opportunity for a hearing for the person to appear in order to show cause why the hardship registration shall not be revoked.\n\n(b) After the opportunity for a hearing, a hearings examiner shall revoke the person's hardship registration if it is determined that the person operated the vehicle.\n\n(c) In the event a person's hardship registration is revoked, the person shall not be able to obtain another hardship registration during the remaining period of time that the person’s license and registration privileges have been suspended or revoked for the offenses set forth in RSA 261:180, III.\n\nSource. #5027, eff 12-19-90; ss by #6296, eff 7-23-96, EXPIRED: 7-23-04\n\nNew. #8181, eff 9-25-04 (from Saf-C 3003.09); ss by #10085, eff 1-31-12; ss by #13279, eff 10-19-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3000.html"
